WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.875
Daily repairs are grouped as return repairs, in progress,
waiting for parts and waiting for collection.

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:12.667
Use the search field to find a customer, device or order, then
check the device.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.750
Click the stage badge in the order row.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:24.042
In the window, choose the actual progress, such as awaiting
diagnosis, being repaired, or repaired and waiting for
collection.

00:00:24.042 --> 00:00:29.417
Check the stage, add a reason when required, then click the
save button below.

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:35.292
A stage change does not confirm parts arrival, payment or the
return of the device.

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:38.417
Click the follow-up button in the order row.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:47.250
After contacting the customer about the quote, choose the
actual result: quote discussed, no answer, or awaiting a reply
about the quote.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.542
Enter a contact note in the field, then click the matching
result button below.

00:00:52.542 --> 00:00:58.250
This saves a record; it does not send a message or prove the
customer approved the repair.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.292
Open the order details to see the device, parts and follow-up
history.

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:07.042
Device custody and return are separate facts.

00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:10.750
Go back to the list to continue with the next order.
